<speak>Late morning is often better than late afternoon for a planned conversation, provided I know about it beforehand. In the afternoon, something from the warehouse tends to run over, and then I am looking at the clock. I would also prefer not to combine a bank meeting with errands at several other places. I used to think that was efficient, but I arrive with my mind still on the previous appointment. A dedicated visit is calmer. If we meet in person, I can come on a day when I am not rushing back to supervise something. Otherwise, a proper telephone slot like today is easier.</speak>